# Keeps the API image's build context to what the Go build actually reads.
#
# There was no root .dockerignore, so `COPY . .` sent the whole working tree
# — including web/node_modules, which is several hundred megabytes and is
# not read by anything in this image. On a CI runner that is upload time and
# layer-cache churn on every build.
#
# Deliberately conservative: internal/gen is gitignored but REQUIRED (the
# Dockerfile has a guard that fails without it), so nothing here may exclude
# generated code. Only things the Go build provably does not read.
.git
.github
build
web/node_modules
web/dist
web/.vite
